-- title:
--   Original pure-jump stopped reward satisfies every initial-event upper budget
-- statement:
--   For every right-continuous initial-filtration event A, the original pure-jump stopped dividend reward Fk has restricted expected value at most w(x) multiplied by its probability. Prove by finite-grid original negative-jump Poisson compensation, A-weighted predictable martingale differences, generator sign, discounted dividend Stieltjes chronology, ruin/time-zero atoms, and infinite small-jump L1 passage. This eventwise statement yields the conditional expected bound via trimmed-measure order comparison.
-- source:
